<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45748" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭb-absurdus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>somewhat</i> or <i>rather absurd</i>
			(Ciceronian): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sunt illa subabsurda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 67, 274</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subabsurda dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 71, 289</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempus discessūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 16, 3, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incompositus, reconditus et, quo Cicero utitur,
					subabsurdus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 5, 65</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 6, 3, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 3,
				99</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭbabsurdē</span></b> ,
				<i>somewhat absurdly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid subabsurde dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 68, 275</span></i>
			.</div>
